{"at": 640, "stored": [{"role": "user", "text": "Remind me how to solve a quadratic, and what the workbook costs.", "timestamp": 1795251600.628, "row_id": 1}, {"role": "assistant", "text": "A quadratic $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ with $a \\neq 0$ has two roots:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nThe part under the root, \\(b^2 - 4ac\\), is the discriminant. When it is negative, the roots are complex.\n\nThe vertex sits halfway between them:\n\n\\[ x_v = -\\frac{b}{2a} \\]\n\nThe workbook costs $5 and the answer key costs $10. In Markdown, write `$x$` to show a formula.\n\nA typo like $\\sqrt{x$ shows as written.", "timestamp": 1795251600.628001, "row_id": 2}]}
